# Environment variables this project reads. Copy to `.env` and edit if you need
# any of them — every DP_* variable has a working default, so a clean clone runs
# with no `.env` at all.
#
# NOTHING HERE IS LOADED AUTOMATICALLY. There is no python-dotenv dependency and
# no code that reads a `.env` file. Export them yourself:
#
#     set -a; . ./.env; set +a
#
# Defaults below are shown as they are computed, not as literals: `${DP_REPO_ROOT}`
# means "derived from the repository root", which is itself derived from where the
# `dpcode` package is installed.


# --- Where the repository is -------------------------------------------------

# Absolute path of the clone. Default: the directory containing the installed
# `dpcode` package, which is correct after `pip install -e .`. Set it explicitly
# if you installed non-editably, or to point the test harness at a fixture tree.
# DP_REPO_ROOT=/path/to/dp-code


# --- Where the data and outputs live -----------------------------------------
# Set these three on a cluster where scratch and datasets are not inside the
# clone. Everything else in `dpcode/conf/paths/default.yaml` is derived from them.

# Cohort data: WSI features and CNV matrices. ~105 GB for everything the
# reproduction path needs (REPRODUCING.md section B.0); more if you also pull the
# CPTAC slides and the dormant RNA modality, neither of which any reported number
# uses. Default: ${DP_REPO_ROOT}/.datasets
# DP_DATA_ROOT=/mnt/scratch/$USER/.datasets

# Derived artifacts: CLAM runs, CNV tabular inputs, external-validation outputs.
# Default: ${DP_REPO_ROOT}/.scratch
# DP_SCRATCH_ROOT=/mnt/scratch/$USER/dp-code

# CLAM run directories. Default: ${DP_SCRATCH_ROOT}/results
# DP_RESULTS_ROOT=/mnt/scratch/$USER/dp-code/results


# --- Other cohort roots ------------------------------------------------------

# Parked cohort — see docs/parked-cohorts/histology-hsi-bc.md.
# Default: ${DP_DATA_ROOT}/HistologyHSI-BC-Recurrence
# DP_HSI_BC_ROOT=

# No default. Leave unset unless you have been given the path.
# DP_NOU_ROOT=


# --- Credentials -------------------------------------------------------------

# HuggingFace access token. Required only for the two GATED MahmoodLab
# repositories: `MahmoodLab/UNI2-h-features` (the pre-extracted WSI features for
# both cohorts) and `MahmoodLab/UNI2-h` (the encoder itself, needed only to tile
# new slides). Request access on the hub first; a token alone is not enough.
# HF_TOKEN=

# Weights & Biases. The API key is NOT set here — it is read from `~/.netrc`,
# which `docker/run.sh` and the devcontainer bind-mount into the container.
#
# The config group is `tracking`, not `wandb`: `tracking=online`,
# `tracking=offline`, `tracking="off"` (quote it — bare `off` is a YAML 1.1
# boolean, and it is the default). The group is named that way because
# `.gitignore` carries a bare `wandb` pattern, which matches a directory of that
# name at any depth, so a `dpcode/conf/wandb/` group could never be committed.
#
# `tracking` configures dpcode's own entry points. It does NOT reach CLAM:
# training runs log to W&B from `clam.wandb` / `clam.wandb_project` /
# `clam.wandb_tags`, which is what the shell wrappers passed. `dp-train` warns on
# stderr if you select a tracking mode while `clam.wandb` is false. To train
# without W&B:  dp-train experiment=... clam.wandb=false
#
# WANDB_MODE: online | offline | disabled. Honoured by `tracking=online`;
# `tracking="off"` forces `disabled` regardless. Use `disabled` in CI and for
# smoke runs.
# WANDB_MODE=online

# Default: clam-brca-subtyping-cv
# WANDB_PROJECT=

# Default: unset (your personal entity).
# WANDB_ENTITY=
